cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Memvine in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Memvine: memory for AI agents"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Gupta"
    given-names: "Vishal"
repository-code: "https://github.com/memvine/memvine"
url: "https://memvine.dev"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
abstract: >-
  Memvine reads each AI agent session, keeps the few things that stay true, with their source,
  and briefs the next agent. It has two modes: a coding mode that keeps little for a team's coding
  agents, and a conversation mode that stores one person's conversation whole beside a small
  profile. Memories about code are rechecked when that code changes.
keywords:
  - agent memory
  - AI agents
  - coding agents
  - MCP
  - long-term memory
